<title>POLAND: Polish food prices rise 0.1 pct October 1-10.</title>
<headline>Polish food prices rise 0.1 pct October 1-10.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish food prices rose 0.1 percent in the October 1-10 period after rising 1.0 percent in the previous 10 days and were 2.4 percent higher than in the September 1-10 period, the Central Statistical Office said.</p>
<p>				   OCT 1-10   SEPT 21-30   LAST 30 DAYS</p>
<p> POLISH FOOD PRICES (AVG)     0.1	   1.0	  2.4  (3.7)</p>
<p>  Bread			     1.2	   0.2	  1.5  (0.4)</p>
<p>  Fruit and vegetables	 -7.8	   4.0	 -0.4  (5.7)</p>
<p>  Meat and meat-products	0.7	   1.4	  4.8  (7.9)</p>
<p>  Dairy products		  0.3	   0.2	  0.7  (0.6)</p>
<p>  Eggs				2.9	   0.7	  4.7  (0.7)</p>
<p>NOTE: In brackets figures for the previous 30-day period ending on September 30.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
